\newlabel{fig:waterfall}{{2}{4}{\textbf {Where this survey searched, and where a repeat could test it}: independent systems covering each sky frequency, one panel per populated ALMA band, its width proportional to the band's frequency share; curves step at the searched window edges. \emph {(a)}~Every window: blue, the fine-channel carrier search (Class~A); grey, the coarse-channel spectral-excess search (Class~B); the summed window bandwidth is $\GrossOverUnion \times $ the union. \emph {(b)}~Class~A: detectable once (grey); with a \emph {separated} block (\S \ref {sec:summary}) covering the frequency (blue); beyond a year (dark). An accelerating carrier further needs a predicted frequency within the repeat coverage, with adequate sensitivity. \emph {(c)}~Class~A systems in which a carrier of that EIRP reaches the threshold nine times in ten in one epoch; dashed, $\CovEirpRefTex $\,W}{figure.2.2}{}}
